title The water row tastes the loops -- the launcher audit answers, %344 books, and the fn macro gets its standing guard
prompt Keaton's kg with all recommended doors granted, plus a direct ask: commands for updating the Silence and Mind launch loops and any others, unless their inner loops already pull latest updates and instructions. Silence's own lap report rode along; its loop ended at 15:18:33.
think N=3748 gave row 3 -- water, a fresh row, read whole: the threshold (taste works up close; sip the actual code), the shape-you-grew fusion (Gall and Conway; this tree's channel IS its written artifacts, since the agents share no memory), the happy zone (contract checks at every seam turn path multiplication into addition), and growing-a-language (five moves; the parity gate is the specification). The movement then lived each seat.
think The launcher audit, measured from the loop lines themselves: Silence, Hush, and Dream all print a while-recipe whose every iteration runs sh tools/f/fleet_round_open.sh (the TREE pulls fresh each lap) and whose seat prompt commands the lap to read ITINERARY whole (so card and rule updates flow in live) -- but the seat_prompt string interpolates ONCE when the launcher prints, so launcher-prompt changes reach a loop only at relaunch. Mind is the exception both ways: tools/l/chatgpt-mind.sh runs an internal while over run_lap, which verifies repository state and never pulls -- its clone goes stale until a hand pulls it. Mystery's launcher carries no loop line of the standard family. Verdict: no running loop needs interruption for BASE updates; relaunch is for ended loops and prompt-text changes; Mind wants a hand-pull before each run.
think REDS %344 booked shelf-born, CLOSED at booking: the almanac's charter promised a close at sixty-four findings and the book held 127 with no note -- the count-cadence lesson one room over from the seed's own CUT, caught by the doc-surface survey, repaired by the dated amendment in commit 83301e6d9. The recital line rides; the pin's headline republished to Rows: 344 and the monotone witness came back GREEN after refusing the stale headline exactly as its happy-zone comment says it exists to do.
think The fn-drift guard family seats the parity-witness door: tools/fixtures/w/wire_lab_fn_drift_scan.sh reads the 15 orchestrators against the teaching head (comlink_device_wire_lab.rish) rather than a recited template -- a deliberate family edit passes, one file wandering reds -- and gates fn_drift and raw_sites at zero; the control proves 12 of 12 behaviors with every refusal planted and freed; tools/w/wire_lab_fn_drift_witness.rish GREEN first run. The happy zone holds the daily check under a second; the thin edge (a real qemu boot) stays with the labs' own gating witnesses.
obs On touch, the water row's dual seat was swept under the first-resident ban: foundations/20260618-184912_growing-a-language.md carried dogfood three times in living prose; the five-moves list now reads live in it as first resident, and the closing circle reads no finer first residency. The child-keeps-watch sentence keeps its child -- family prose, where warmth outranks uniformity by the rule's own carve-out.
obs Receipt tags from the row's six: the launcher audit was taste (sip the actual loop line); the %344 booking was tide (a finding returning on its own rhythm to the ledger); the fn guard is nectar (a seam proven sweet and kept sweet); and the wayland tri-OS close stays longing, named without rushing.
